EXTRA["unit-price-math"] = """
<h2>A quick mental shortcut</h2>
<p>You do not always need a calculator. If one pack is twice the size of another, it should cost less than twice as much to be the better deal. If a bundle of three costs more than three singles on sale, skip the bundle. For awkward sizes, round both to a common quantity: compare a 14-ounce box with a 20-ounce box by asking what 10 ounces of each would cost. These rough checks catch most bad bundles in the aisle, and you can confirm the close calls with your phone. Over a year of weekly shopping, quietly picking the lower unit price on the items you buy most often tends to add up to more than chasing occasional big-ticket discounts.</p>
"""

